#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:1
msgid "Release 2.14 (2023-02-28)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:3
msgid ""
"A new function `builtins.readFileType` is available. It is similar to "
"`builtins.readDir` but acts on a single file or directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:6
msgid ""
"In flakes, the `.outPath` attribute of a flake now always refers to the "
"directory containing the `flake.nix`. This was not the case for when `flake."
"nix` was in a subdirectory of e.g. a Git repository. The root of the source "
"of a flake in a subdirectory is still available in `.sourceInfo.outPath`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:12
msgid ""
"In derivations that use structured attributes, you can now use "
"`unsafeDiscardReferences` to disable scanning a given output for runtime "
"dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:18
msgid ""
"This is useful e.g. when generating self-contained filesystem images with "
"their own embedded Nix store: hashes found inside such an image refer to the "
"embedded store and not to the host's Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:22
msgid "This requires the `discard-references` experimental feature."
msgstr ""
